    explanation="In string, prefix asks about the front of the character sequence. On a route, 'does this road start in my town' is the same question about the front of a sequence of stops -- queens is on the road but not at the start. In algebra, the prefix relation on the free monoid is the order relation generated by 'can be extended to'. All three share: a sequence, a candidate head, an answer that depends on position and not just membership.",
